WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.094
<v Examiner>Two marks.

2
00:00:02.094 --> 00:00:07.976
<v Examiner>Identify and describe one ethical consideration of a patient taking part in a clinical

3
00:00:07.976 --> 00:00:08.386
<v Examiner>trial.

4
00:00:08.836 --> 00:00:12.066
Identify and describe, so name it, then describe it.

5
00:00:12.066 --> 00:00:13.867
Her answer: informed consent.

6
00:00:13.867 --> 00:00:19.458
The patient must know the trial's purpose, its potential benefits and its potential risks,

7
00:00:19.458 --> 00:00:24.427
in her scenario to the mother and the unborn baby, before agreeing to take part.

8
00:00:24.427 --> 00:00:29.334
Or: she can withdraw her consent at any time, even after agreeing at the start,

9
00:00:29.334 --> 00:00:30.639
with no consequences.

10
00:00:31.089 --> 00:00:33.243
The phases, for the multi-choice.

11
00:00:33.243 --> 00:00:36.443
Preclinical: no humans, the lab and then animals.

12
00:00:36.443 --> 00:00:39.512
Phase one: a small group of healthy volunteers.

13
00:00:39.512 --> 00:00:41.210
Is it safe, and what dose?

14
00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:43.626
Phase two: people with the condition.

15
00:00:43.626 --> 00:00:46.499
Does it work, and what are the side effects?

16
00:00:46.499 --> 00:00:47.739
Often double-blind.

17
00:00:47.739 --> 00:00:50.808
Phase three: large groups, often international.

18
00:00:50.808 --> 00:00:53.159
Is it better than current treatment?

19
00:00:53.159 --> 00:00:55.771
Phase four: post-marketing surveillance,

20
00:00:55.771 --> 00:01:00.276
watching everyone who's prescribed it for problems the trials missed.

21
00:01:00.276 --> 00:01:02.692
A drug can be withdrawn at any phase.

22
00:01:03.142 --> 00:01:03.847
Three more.

23
00:01:03.847 --> 00:01:08.913
Bioequivalent: two drugs or brands with the same rate and extent of absorption,

24
00:01:08.913 --> 00:01:11.542
which is how a generic matches the brand.

25
00:01:11.542 --> 00:01:17.249
New Zealand is one of the few countries that allow medicines to be advertised directly to

26
00:01:17.249 --> 00:01:21.289
the public, so people ask for brands by name: an ethical issue.

27
00:01:21.289 --> 00:01:25.073
And the evidence pyramid has systematic reviews at the top.

28
00:01:25.523 --> 00:01:31.000
Clinical trial ethics: informed consent, purpose, benefits and risks before agreeing;

29
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:33.448
and the right to withdraw at any time.

30
00:01:33.448 --> 00:01:38.539
Phases: preclinical in the lab; one, healthy volunteers, safety; two, patients,

31
00:01:38.539 --> 00:01:44.338
does it work; three, large groups, better than current; four, post-marketing surveillance.

32
00:01:44.338 --> 00:01:47.560
Bioequivalent: same rate and extent of absorption.
